# AnnPocketDb :: ci/ubsan.supp
#
# UBSan suppressions. UBSan is cheap and precise (integer overflow,
# misaligned loads, invalid enum values, signed-shift UB) -- there is almost
# never a legitimate reason to suppress a hit inside project code. If
# something here fires inside the vendored Monocypher C source
# (thirdparty/monocypher/monocypher.c), check first whether upstream already
# has a documented "this is intentional, constant-time-safe UB" note before
# suppressing; if so, reference it in the entry.
#
# Example:
# signed-integer-overflow:thirdparty/monocypher/monocypher.c

# (intentionally empty)
